  "prefLabel": "Alc 406.05 Obligations of Supervisors",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Alc 406.05 Obligations of Supervisors. Clinical supervisors of MLADCs and candidates for initial licensure as a MLADC shall:\n\n(a) Obtain a copy of the board approval letter for the supervisory agreement from the candidate for initial MLADC licensure before beginning supervision;\n\n(b) Become familiar with Alc 406 before beginning to provide clinical supervision;\n\n(c) If temporarily unable to perform supervision, ensure that a substitute supervisor who meets the eligibility standards of Alc 405.02 is available to continue supervision; and\n\n(d) Maintain records of supervision for a period no less than 7 years after the termination of the supervision.\n\nSource. #12548, eff 7-1-18; ss by #14045, eff 10-7-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/alc100-500.html"
